# Where the CAD fixture sits in the robot base frame. Edit and save: the publisher re-reads this file every 2 s, RViz updates by itself.
# Nominal CAD placement: cradle plugs at x = 0.25 m (USB y = -0.05 m), socket board at x = 0.55 m. Initial offset = camera-measured USB plug (0.2707, -0.0150) minus the CAD plug (0.250, -0.050);
# z offset puts the cradle bottom on the measured table height. Tune by eye against the live camera cloud, then keep the numbers.
# Nominal CAD placement, no offset: what the design says. Compare the live cloud against this to measure the camera mapping.
# Earlier fit to one cloud (single arm pose, not trusted): offset_m [0.0196, 0.0309, 0.0175], yaw_deg 1.17 (kept in fixture_pose.yaml.fitted)
anchor_m: [0.25, -0.05, 0.0]
offset_m: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
yaw_deg: 0.0
